{"school":{"dbn":"20K201","name":"J.H.S. 201 The Madeleine Brennan School","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"20","district_label":"District 20","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":1526,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"8010 12 AVENUE, BROOKLYN, NY 11228","phone":"718-633-8200","website":null,"directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/66354","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"\"Academic Excellence Is the Key to Success\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u009d; and at The Madeleine Brennan School, we strive for success every day. For the upcoming school year, we are proud to be offering a Superintendent  Legal Studies program, a Dual Language Program in Italian and a Dual Language program. In addition to these programs, we provide students with Project Based Learning opportunities through our STEAM programs, teach student advocacy through our AVID program, and provide rigorous standards aligned instruction that meets the needs of our diverse student population. We encourage our students to work hard, explore new interests, develop positive relationships, and build on existing strengths. The school offers a variety of programs and resources during and after school to enrich each child's overall development. We rely heavily on our parent partnerships. This is achieved through the school website, GAMA emails and texts, NYCSA, parent engagement activities, and the PTA. The Madeleine Brennan School strives to prepare your child to be college- and career-ready, but ultimately, give your child the foundation to be successful in all of their future endeavors.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"B1, B16, B4, B64, B70, X28, X38","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Dyker Heights","latitude":40.618558,"longitude":-74.013309,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_